  "description": "Ginger adds heat to this tart kale limeade. Apple juice and coconut water tame the intense flavor—think of this as green juice for beginners—it's friendly, fun, and a little (naturally) sweet.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Garnish: lime slices\n\nNotes: This recipe yields about 3 cups of juice, enough for two 1 1/2-cup servings.\nIn our testing, it took about 0.68 kg of kale to produce 1 cup of juice. Results may vary based on kale and on juicer.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Juice is best served immediately and will lost flavor and color with time. Store leftover juice in a sealed container in the refrigerator for up to 1 day.",
